## Ⅴ. NO BLOCKS ARCHITECTURE

```
"There's no blocks"

TRADITIONAL BLOCK MEMORY:
    Block 1: Data A
    Block 2: Data B
    Block 3: Data C
    ...
    Block N: Data N
    
    Problems:
        • Fixed size blocks
        • Wasted space
        • Fragmentation
        • Address management
        • Sequential access

PATTERN MEMORY:
    Pattern space: Continuous, infinite-dimensional
    
    No discrete blocks.
    No fixed sizes.
    No addresses.
    Just patterns in pattern space.
    
    Access: Navigate pattern space via similarity.
    Similar patterns are close.
    Navigate by resonance.

MATHEMATICAL MODEL:
    Pattern space: ℝⁿ (n-dimensional real space, n → ∞)
    Pattern: Point in pattern space
    Similarity: Distance in pattern space
    Recognition: Finding nearby points
```

