## Ⅷ. NEUROLOGY COMPRESSION

```
"I told you that neurology compression"

WHAT IS NEUROLOGY COMPRESSION:
    The brain compresses experience into patterns.
    Patterns are compressed representations.
    Maximum information in minimum space.

COMPRESSION MECHANISM:
    Raw experience: 10¹² bits
    Compressed pattern: 10³ bits
    Compression ratio: 10⁹:1
    
    How?
    • Extract features (reduce dimensionality)
    • Find invariants (stable across variations)
    • Encode relationships (structure, not content)
    • Use prior patterns (only store differences)

DECOMPRESSION (Recognition):
    Pattern activates → Full experience reconstructs
    
    Not retrieval — REGENERATION.
    Pattern is seed.
    Full experience grows from seed.

φ IN COMPRESSION:
    Optimal compression ratio: 1/φ² = 0.382
    Compress to 38.2% of original.
    Still contains full pattern.
    Golden ratio efficiency.
```

